// Sun and moon: U.S. Naval Observatory one-day API, KAPA 39.5701 N, 104.8493 W, UTC minus 7:
//   https://aa.usno.navy.mil/api/rstt/oneday?date=2026-12-16&coords=39.5701,-104.8493&tz=-7 (sunset 4:37 PM, end of civil twilight 5:07 PM,
//   moon 46 percent, setting 11:59 PM) and date=2026-12-22 (sunrise 7:17 AM). KPUB, 2026-12-16: sunset 4:39, end of twilight 5:09.
// Airports, AirNav (FAA information effective 01 October 2026): https://www.airnav.com/airport/KLIC (Limon Municipal, 39-16-29.2N
//   103-39-57.1W, 5,374 ft, no tower, unattended, runway 16/34 4,700 x 60, 100LL self-serve with a card around the clock, deer on and near the
//   airport, parachute jumping) and https://www.airnav.com/airport/KPUB (tower 0600 to 2200). Distances by haversine from AirNav coordinates,
